UMR-5T human MRI

This BIDS dataset contains MRI recordings from eight participants acquired at
5 tesla. It includes 54 NIfTI images: eight T1-weighted, seven T2-weighted,
seven FLAIR, nine resting-state BOLD runs, nine BOLD reverse-encoding reference
images, seven diffusion-weighted runs, and seven diffusion reverse-encoding
reference images. Participant sub-01 has two BOLD runs and a T1-weighted image;
the other seven participants have one BOLD run and all three structural contrasts.
Scout images, clinical reports, derived diffusion maps, and the additional TOF
acquisition are not included in this release. Acquisition parameters and
fieldmap associations are provided in the JSON sidecars.

De-identification and image preparation

Acquisition dates, equipment serial identifiers and nonessential free-text
metadata have been omitted. NIfTI free-text fields and extensions have been
removed. Original DICOM files are not distributed.

All 22 structural images have been defaced. The FSL defacing mask was estimated
on a temporary 1 mm T1-weighted copy and transferred to the native image grid
with nearest-neighbour interpolation. For T2-weighted and FLAIR images, rigid
registration to the temporary T1-weighted copy was used only to transfer the
binary mask. The released structural images retain their original voxel grid,
affine, data type and intensity scaling; values inside the retained region are
bitwise unchanged, and masked voxels are set to zero. Temporary resampled
images, masks and registration matrices are not part of this dataset.

Orthogonal before/after images were visually checked for facial removal and
unintended brain removal. This sampled visual check is not an exhaustive
segmentation-based assessment. Functional, diffusion and reference image
voxel arrays were not resampled or otherwise preprocessed during packaging.

